-- Passage wg5-writing-with-evidence-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f4cd98ea-1d21-5ddd-a6a2-75f583d33f36', 'wg5-writing-with-evidence-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Draft: Planning a Shadow Puppet Show$q$, $q$(1) In "Stories in the Light," Kenji Watanabe explains how shadow puppet shows are made. (2) Watanabe shows that a shadow puppet show needs careful planning, not just a good story. (3) First, he explains that puppet makers cut figures from thick paper or thin leather. (4) They punch tiny holes in the figures so that dots of light shine through and show details like eyes and buttons. (5) ____.

(6) Watanabe also writes about the light. (7) The lamp must sit behind the puppets, and the screen must be in front of them. (8) If a puppet moves closer to the screen, its shadow gets sharper and smaller. (9) If it moves toward the lamp, the shadow grows bigger and blurrier. (10) Puppeteers use this trick to make a character seem to walk toward the audience.

(11) Finally, the puppeteers must practice together. (12) Watanabe describes one show where three people moved eleven puppets. (13) He says they rehearsed every scene until they could move without bumping into each other in the dark.$q$, 'draft')
