        '3-5', $q$Draft: The Library on Wheels$q$, $q$(1) In "The Library on Wheels," Rosa Delgado writes about a bookmobile that visits small towns in her county. (2) A bookmobile is a large van filled with shelves of books. (3) Delgado shows that the bookmobile brings reading and more to families who live far from a library.

(4) ____. (5) Delgado explains that the nearest library is forty miles from some of the farms on the route. (6) Many families cannot make that drive every week. (7) The bookmobile stops in each town every Tuesday. (8) This means children can get new books as often as kids who live in the city.

(9) The bookmobile also offers more than books. (10) Delgado writes that it carries two laptops that visitors can use to do homework or look for jobs. (11) The driver also reads a story aloud at each stop. (12) My favorite book is about a dragon who learns to bake. (13) These details show that the bookmobile is a place for the whole community.$q$, 'draft')
