   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (2) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Haddad shows that tardigrades can survive conditions that would harm most living things.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Moss is a small green plant that grows in shady places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Haddad shows that tardigrades are the strongest animals on Earth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"Tardigrades have eight short legs with tiny claws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Haddad shows that tardigrades can survive conditions that would harm most living things.$q$, $q$Both body paragraphs describe hard conditions tardigrades survive, so this claim fits the draft. Nothing in the draft compares their strength with every animal on Earth, so that choice goes too far.$q$, 'draft', 'c7bb7079-9eaa-595b-bffb-6e5e1aa8ee39')
